{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>יְבִיאֶהָ אֵת תְּרוּמַת ה'</b> — like 'יָבִיא אֶת תְּרוּמַת ה', but with a denominative and explicative sense. So too 'וַתִּפְתַּח וַתִּרְאֵהוּ אֶת הַיֶּלֶד' (Exodus 2:6), 'בְּבוֹאוֹ הָאִישׁ' (Ezekiel 10:3), 'אֲשֶׁר לֹא יַעַבְדוּ אֹתוֹ אֶת נְבוּכַדְנֶצַּר' (Jeremiah 27:8), 'אֲשֶׁר אָנֹכִי נֹתֵן לָהֶם לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל' (Joshua 1:2), and many like these. And by way of truth it is like 'יְבִיאֶהָ עִם תְּרוּמַת ה', (Zohar Vayakhel 198a), that he brings the supernal terumah, in the sod of 'וְיִקְחוּ לִי תְּרוּמָה' (Exodus 25:2), which I have already explained (Ramban on Exodus 25:3). And for our Sages it is a midrash on 'וַתִּפְתַּח וַתִּרְאֵהוּ אֶת הַיֶּלֶד' (Exodus 2:6), that she saw the Shekhinah with him (Sotah 12b). Now Moses needed to relate to the entire congregation all the work that HaShem had commanded him, in order to inform them that they needed to bring a great donation, for the work was great. Therefore he told them <b>הַמִּשְׁכָּן אֶת אָהֳלוֹ וְאֶת מִכְסֵהוּ וְגוֹ'</b> — he mentioned all of them in general terms. And the sense of <b>אֶת הַמִּשְׁכָּן</b>, <b>אֶת הָאָרוֹן</b>, <b>אֶת הַשֻּׁלְחָן</b>, and all those mentioned, with the definite article, is as if saying 'the Tabernacle and the implements' — which we shall designate to the wise men who do the work in their specifics and measurements, for now to the entire congregation he tells them only by their names in general.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {0 "The phrase 'בְּהֵ\"א הַיְּדִיעָה' refers to the definite article prefixed to each item; the 'ה' is the definite article."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:19:45.960342697Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}